  "introText": "Hey guys! I’m BUDDY! Today, we’ll practice endings that decide where the strong syllable of a word goes. They’re... …WORD ENDINGS! The syllable before the ending is the strong one: decision\n\n-tion, -sion, -ture and -ous are always weak, and they pull the stress back. Stressing the ending is the single most Brazilian-sounding habit in long words.",
